{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/576765-ways-other-splats-can-reduce-torment","id":576765,"title":"Ways other splats can reduce Torment?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-02T14:15:37-07:00","id":576765,"title":"Ways other splats can reduce Torment?","content":"Wraiths have Castigation, Hollow Ones have a spell in their book that is basically a different form of Castigation using a &quot;Fetter Ball&quot; as a focus, and Mummies have &quot;Sin-Eating&quot; where the Target tells you his dark desires which you repeat thus taking them onto yourself and away from the target. <br /> <br /> If you were going to allow crossovers which, for Wraith, is already a must, which powers used to reduce the darkness in another would you allow to help the Fallen?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T15:36:55-07:00","id":576816,"title":"","content":"WHO HAS SUMMON THE ALMIGHTY AND POWERFUL CROWLEY!<br /> <br /> Oh, hey mercurial...<br /> <br /> So, technically speaking i belive theres NO WAY to get your permanent torment down...BUT, but<br /> I belive that in the player's guide is stated that is possible to get a permanent point lower for 10 exp only IF your termporal torment goes down.<br /> Character wise, basically make him do Good Things.<br /> <br /> CROWLEY HAS SPOKEN!!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T00:20:43-07:00","id":577123,"title":"","content":"But what about the special abilities of other splats, such as Mummies Sin-Eating or the Shaman ability to summon the spirit of your targets mental sickness and do battle with it? I am not talking about Permanent Torment, though I suspect a steady regime of having it gnawed away by a Sin-Eater might have an effect, but what about bleeding off Temporary Torment?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T07:32:44-07:00","id":577339,"title":"","content":"Not terribly familiar with the Demon rules, but my understanding is that they're immune to mind control and supernatural emotion-manipulating effects from most other splats. It seems like that would apply to effects beneficial to them as well as things that go against their will.<br /> <br /> Then again, I suppose a mage with enough dots in Mind and/or Spirit can make metaphysical changes in anything, so there's at least a possibility by going that route.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T15:51:10-07:00","id":577886,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure it is Mind control. It's more like when demons eat each other. A better way to look at it is the Grondir, who ate the spiritual corruption out of others. This is a transference of the spiritual corruption from one being to another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T16:42:22-07:00","id":577947,"title":"","content":"theres no way to rip the Torment out of a demon through &quot;Outside Help.&quot;<br /> <br /> And even if it Was...torment is..Complex. The Way I SEE IT, torment is something that is pure evil and madness to an almost lovecraftian level, something that only the High agents of the Wyrm and Oblivion would TRY to comprehend and yet fail to it.<br /> <br /> I feel like any supernatural beeing must have a basic comprehention of &quot; What they are trying to cure you from &quot;. but in this case is an element so Alien thats pretty much impossible with out creating a World of Pain and Suffering to the one involved...<br /> <br /> a mage tried to get my demon rid of torment (even if it was a score of 5), the ST made the player's mage be driven utterly insane and even tried to rip his own eyes off due the sheer horror of what a demon has to experience every day thanks to the torment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T17:37:41-07:00","id":577994,"title":"","content":"The thing is, Torment isn't precisely a spiritual corruption. That is what makes it different from even (inverse)Humanity in wich it is based.<br /> <br /> Torment is, from the start, the simple spite, hate and resentment from the Fallen. It is a literal Hell of a LOT of negative emotions, but still NATURAL negative emotions. They don't affect the Fallen because they are spiritual corruption, but because the Fallen themselfes are ephemeral beings to begin with.<br /> <br /> Rules-wise, such a thing wouldn't work. Obeah, maybe, since it can restore Humanity to a Mortal, so theoreticaly could cleanse common bitterness, but I wouldn't allow it without heinous difficulty. The Fallen endured more pain than any other creature, save Caine itself and other insanely old chars. Maybe. Either way, no rule exist to do that.<br /> <br /> If you want, you could let such a thing work just to levy the XP cost (I never liked the XP cost on this kind of trait), but work to keep all the roleplay difficulties of doing so, or even rising them.<br /> <br /> In the end, more than most other things, do whatever works for you. Torment is a trait with (relatively) few to no impact on the rules and game balance, it exists for the experience of the drama. So you will not really mess anything on the game if you take another approach on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T19:50:23-07:00","id":578066,"title":"","content":"cough...ephemera it's not a concept of Demon...cough...<br /> <br /> I concur with the general idea of Torment being unhealable by any other thing that good actions, (or God's forgiveness). The very fact that Demons can't just &quot;heal&quot; it should be proof enough that Torment isn't suposed to work that way.<br /> However, if you want to play with the crossover idea that &quot;Mages can do anything&quot;. I think it should be treated in a similar manner as the healing of vampirism.<br /> <br /> That it's, do it BIG. Make it so not &quot;any&quot; mage can face such darkness without turning suicidal crazy, or being overwhelmed with Jhor. Only mages immensely powerful, wise, and probably insane, with some serious understanding of the Elohim, should be able to do such a thing (so the demon needs to find a truly wise and scary mage to do it).<br /> <br /> Also, the &quot;Torment healing&quot; should be more than a mere removal of temporal points. You can make it to be as dramatic as you want. Like making the mage create a construct where the metaphysical essence of anger and ungodliness that it's the Torment manifest itself, which the demon has to face, in an Umbrascape. Even then, Permanent Torment shouldn't be banished without expending at least some experience points, to preserve the system (albeit this very &quot;sesion&quot; could justify investing them, if dramatic enough).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T00:39:56-07:00","id":578374,"title":"","content":"Thanks to all who answered. Everyone of you gave great answers, and much to think about. Torment has bothered me a little because it is so easy to accrue and once you hit 10 your utterly damned. I liked the notion of a game that at some point dealt with looking through the WOD for some sort of cure or therapy. In retrospect, I doubt Sin-Eating would work for anyone besides Osiris. Still, I would like to brainstorm a way of finding a cure that would allow a well meaning Fallen heal an old comrade that went Earth Bound or was captured and subjected to the Tormented version of Voice of Heaven until there was nothing left to save. <br /> <br /> A wizard doing it might seem like the smart bet, although it should probably be done by proxy via Artifacts/Inventions and Charms/Gadgets. But I'm still not sure what kind of therapy would work. I suppose it WOULD be similar to curing vampirism, but I am just not sure where to start or how it would work. Even Oblivion doesn't feel strong enough to choke down what the Fallen are trying to unburden themselves of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 07-04-2015, 03:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T02:28:35-07:00","id":578468,"title":"","content":"No, ephemera is not a concept of Demon. It is just another word for spirit-matter or whatever-non-material-stuff. And Demons ARE made of whatever-non-material-stuff, at least now. So...<br /> <br /> I wouldn't make it so hard on normal Torment levels. Again, the most similar trait, even if described on other terms, is a vampire's Humanity. Surely, lowing from Torment 10 should be as hard as rising from Humanity 0, the dreaded Wassail. By the way, that was done before, I remember at least one instance. Lowering TO Torment 0 should be at least as hard as reaching Golconda. That was ALSO done before. MAYBE it is as hard as curing vampirism.<br /> <br /> But not so to any oher level of Torment.<br /> <br /> My point is, in this case a middle ground isn't a good one to stand. Lowering Torment isn't such a great thing aside such extremes. It's 10 XP. You can judge roleplay before letting it be done, you can make a touching scene about redemption and forgiveness, but in the end is just 10 XP. It is cheaper than Humanity, by the way, even being described as way more terrifying than the Beast.<br /> <br /> So, if you make that an incredibly hard quest for the right person, place and artifact, just to in the end take the XP as said in the book, the player will have reason to feel cheated. The quest will have the SOLE purpose of XP economy, because that's the only thing the rules demand, XP. Of course, in a RPG you want to make things have meaning, but such a quest can be overkill for something that the book says how to work around. Not so cheap, nor so hard either.<br /> <br /> You can make it hard and them let it be XP free. You can make it be simple and it will just justify the XP cost. Or you can prohibit it at all, preserving the feeling without harm to the players.<br /> <br /> Outside that, I repeat, Torment is the sum of the natural bad feelings of the Fallen. It taints their powers because they have problems to focus with so much anger. Go read about Torment in the book, it's nothing spectacular except by being a spectacular amount of bad feelings. That means it is not about the Demons being forgiven. It is about THEM forgiving. So anything that could aid in reducing Torment would simply be some sort of huge cathartic experience or the like. It's like therapy, except it would take a therapist able himself to handle a patient hugely messed-up.<br /> <br /> And in the end, it's not about how you low Torment, but about how he character feels after.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T10:26:54-07:00","id":578921,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that's true. I guess Torment sounds more terrible than what actually it's.<br /> <br /> As a way to &quot;pass&quot; the immunity to mind manipulation that Demons have, a <i>very trusting </i>demon might just empty her own Faith reserve...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T17:04:44-07:00","id":579277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/576765-ways-other-splats-can-reduce-torment?p=578468#post578468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wouldn't make it so hard on normal Torment levels. Again, the most similar trait, even if described on other terms, is a vampire's Humanity. Surely, lowing from Torment 10 should be as hard as rising from Humanity 0, the dreaded Wassail. By the way, that was done before, I remember at least one instance. Lowering TO Torment 0 should be at least as hard as reaching Golconda. That was ALSO done before. MAYBE it is as hard as curing vampirism.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, when was someone cured of vampirism?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T17:28:36-07:00","id":579289,"title":"","content":"Was a cross Mage-Vampire, don't remember the title now, but it's cited on the Time of Judgement Ascension book. Some end-of-times stuff. If I recall well, depending on what the players do a lot of shit can come from that.<br /> <br /> Either way, I was talking about Golconda. Achieving Golconda and recovering from Wassail where both done canonicaly before.<br /> <br /> And well thought, Aleph, a trusting Demon could simply spent all Faith points to be mind-affected. To develop such trust, by the way, would be part of the very process of cure. Maybe the ST could use such process to let the player low 2 or more of Torment by the cost of 1, as the Demon finaly let someone enter the deepest recess of his mind to help him let go the suffering.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T23:40:39-07:00","id":579533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/576765-ways-other-splats-can-reduce-torment?p=579277#post579277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait, when was someone cured of vampirism?</div> </div> </div> </div>The whole crossover book <i>The Red Sign</i> was about the attempt to do so. It was treated as a much bigger deal in Revised than it had been in earlier versions of the game. I got the impression that breaking the Curse of Cain via magic in that manner was one of the potential causes of the Withering effect in Gehenna.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T22:54:29-07:00","id":580560,"title":"","content":"Doi! *Smacks self on head?* I meant curing someone of Wassail.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T01:51:53-07:00","id":580664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/576765-ways-other-splats-can-reduce-torment#post576765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wraiths have Castigation, Hollow Ones have a spell in their book that is basically a different form of Castigation using a &amp;quot;Fetter Ball&amp;quot; as a focus, and Mummies have &amp;quot;Sin-Eating&amp;quot; where the Target tells you his dark desires which you repeat thus taking them onto yourself and away from the target. <br /> <br /> If you were going to allow crossovers which, for Wraith, is already a must, which powers used to reduce the darkness in another would you allow to help the Fallen?</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, it's a must for wraith? Have you played wraith? The only non-wraiths they need to deal with are their fetters (and sources of their passions) and spectres (who are kinda wraiths)... They kinda avoid the other megasplats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T15:12:01-07:00","id":581573,"title":"","content":"Kemintiri was cured from Wassail by the Sons of Osiris on the distant past. No details about it, but was how she learned Bardo. She went from 0 to 3 Humanity before leaving them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T23:06:40-07:00","id":581979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/576765-ways-other-splats-can-reduce-torment?p=580664#post580664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait, it's a must for wraith? Have you played wraith? The only non-wraiths they need to deal with are their fetters (and sources of their passions) and spectres (who are kinda wraiths)... They kinda avoid the other megasplats.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant that, unlike werewolves, wraiths are as much of a package deal for demons as they are for Hunters/Imbued. With werewolves, there is still enough unwritten in the Demon book to say they aren't Garou but something your ST made up. In Demon, they are already talking about Charon the wraith and his reign in Stygia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T01:34:36-07:00","id":585767,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> Lore of Spirits 5 can rip a demon's torment out. &quot;High Torment&quot; version of the Lore but still plausible. If the Demon that does it is high torment their victim gets to soak up all that horror as the demon plays with its soul thus increasing the victim's torment. If the demon is low torment it treats itself as a filter and helps purge the 'victims' torment. If it works one way not much reason it wouldn't work the other even if you're not using the rules RAW.<br /> <br /> Imbued could do it really easily. Demons are explicitly not immune to the Redeemers' &quot;Do you remember?&quot; shit and that is literally the definition of what triggers conscience rolls for torment reduction. Think it was redemption 1 or 2<br /> <br /> Don't see why Obeah/Valeran 5 couldn't do it if a Demon was actually willing to let a vampire hold its spirit. People seem to think that Demons have these vast, dark and twisted memories... But, most don't. Most barely remember shit. The Torment comes from their own, current, rage/hate and refusing to let go. Obeah/Valeran can fix that fairly easily.<br /> <br /> Uh, What else... Mages with Spirit 5 Mind 5 and *maybe* Prime 5 could probably do it. Good luck finding one of those, though. Would think being a master of those 3 spheres would let them bypass the whole &quot;Immune to mind control&quot; thing fairly easily since Demons are demonstrably *not* 100% immune to being controlled given that some asshole who summons them properly is fully capable of binding them into service.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure Kuei Jin have a similar power to Valeran 5 (which iirc Valeran 5 was a copy of) so they could probably do it the same way Salubri could if they were inclined to do so. Going off very vague memories on this one though so might not be that accurate here.<br /> <br /> I have no idea for Wraith powers but I would think anything that can help restore a Specter's sanity (is there such a thing? Idk) would work similarly on a Demon.<br /> <br /> No idea about changelings... Mummies, same.<br /> <br /> Also feel the need to point out all this talk of &quot;10 XP&quot; to reduce Torment is wrong. That only applies if the person is actually buying their Torment down and it takes it down a level flat out. No need for the virtue stuff. IE use it when you have the following scenario: &quot;I have Torment 9 and there's no way in Hell my Virtue rating of 3 can possibly compete with my Torment rating on that roll.&quot; If you are at Torment 4.0 and you pass your conscience check for a good deed you lose your temporary point of torment and go down to 3.9. If Temp Torment didn't effect perm Torment then it couldn't take you from 4.9 to 5 either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4017,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4017-angryicecream","user":"angryicecream","date":". 07-10-2015, 04:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4017-angryicecream","name":"angryicecream","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T14:16:01-07:00","id":586437,"title":"","content":"You're wrong in one thing: the game does say explicit that Temp Torm can raise Perm Torm, but to reduce Perm Torm talks ONLY about XP. So, even if you use that as a rule on your table (and I DO use in mine), it ISN'T the RAW. The official rule IS XP for reducing Perm Torm, and that's it.<br /> <br /> Also, your thoughts on current memories are just partially true. By what's on the book, there are such relation to a degree, but Torm is still a reflection of all that suffering, not just from current memories. Also, when you suck that soul or something, that soul DOES have all the memories, or at least there are no reason for not having them.<br /> <br /> In the end, that's al fluff. That's the important thing to understand. Torment is a fluff, very important for the mod of the game, not so for the rules. If you think in your game it works well to just let it go that easily, I don't think you would need even so much mastery of Spheres. Mind 3 and the Demon without any Faith (to be vulnerable to Mind) should be enough. Spirit 2, at most.<br /> <br /> The difficulties should be there just as long as you want to keep the mood of Torment being a touch of HELL!, with all-caps and an exclamation point. I like this approach, that's all. Just think you shouldn't forget the 10XP cost. Because that does set un upper limit for difficulty: you can prohibit another way to reduce it, but never create a way that is EVEN MORE costly than the default, because the default is there for a reason, and will be there for your players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T21:20:35-07:00","id":590826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/576765-ways-other-splats-can-reduce-torment?p=577123#post577123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But what about the special abilities of other splats, such as Mummies Sin-Eating or the Shaman ability to summon the spirit of your targets mental sickness and do battle with it? I am not talking about Permanent Torment, though I suspect a steady regime of having it gnawed away by a Sin-Eater might have an effect, but what about bleeding off Temporary Torment?<br /> <br /> Torment has bothered me a little because it is so easy to accrue and once you hit 10 your utterly damned. I liked the notion of a game that at some point dealt with looking through the WOD for some sort of cure or therapy. In retrospect, I doubt Sin-Eating would work for anyone besides Osiris. Still, I would like to brainstorm a way of finding a cure that would allow a well meaning Fallen heal an old comrade that went Earth Bound or was captured and subjected to the Tormented version of Voice of Heaven until there was nothing left to save.<br /> <br /> A wizard doing it might seem like the smart bet, although it should probably be done by proxy via Artifacts/Inventions and Charms/Gadgets. But I'm still not sure what kind of therapy would work. I suppose it WOULD be similar to curing vampirism, but I am just not sure where to start or how it would work. Even Oblivion doesn't feel strong enough to choke down what the Fallen are trying to unburden themselves of.</div> </div> </div> </div>Torment is the psychological trauma all Fallen deal with in having been responsible for the destruction and decay of the world, people, and things they loved most dearly. They know that their actions brought this about, making them tragic heroes not unlike Dracula or Sweeney Todd. On top of that, they were thrown into the pit where they descended into madness and turned upon one another in the most terrible psychic warfare as they were left with nothing to think about save their failures for an eternity. Torment is an intense psychological agony, one that no other being can say they have equally suffered, but it is still only that. It is the grief and madness that has come as the cost of what they have done and what they loved. It is an eternity of suffering.<br /> <br /> That said, I think the straight up XP cost system of reducing Torment blows. I think it needs to be RP-ed down, and I think there are things you could do that would improve the rate you could diminish it! I think that reducing Torment eventually needs to come down to some nature of roll (with the difficulty set at your current Torment). If your Demon can find someone to talk to about their suffering, that should help. Literally, going into therapy for it! But... it would need to be someone who could at least partially relate to your suffering, someone who could understand the decisions or the supernatural dimension of your story, and someone whose Torment was lower than yours (or if it's a vampire, someone whose Humanity is greater than 10 - your Torment). If your character is attending therapy once a week with someone who can help you and listen to you, like a Hunter Redeemer or a Shih or someone who can believe all you have to say, then once per week I'd allow that character roll Charisma + Empathy (difficulty equal to your Permanent Torment) to reduce your Temporary Torment by one point.<br /> <br /> The rules are sketchy... they say you can reduce Temporary Torment with acts of Kindness, and then say that you can reduce Permanent Torment with Experience.... and imply acts of kindness can also do it O.o<br /> <br /> I would say that you can reduce Permanent Torment by lowering your Temporary Torment to zero. Then, if you would reduce it by another point of Temporary Torment you reduce your Permanent Torment by 1 and gain 9 Temporary Torment. The same applies to the use of therapy (if your Temporary Torment is zero, and therapy would reduce it again then gain 9 Temporary Torment and reduce your Permanent Torment by 1).<br /> <br /> Hunters in particular have an extraordinary connection to Demons! Their powers are alike, and Hunter edges impact Demons more so than other things in the WoD.... some demons abuse that sameness and pervert Hunters, which is how we can know they are related in origin. Anyway, Redeemers do have powers that could help with this sort of thing. I'd say the level 2 Redeemer Edge, Insight (out of the Creed book), would be able to help a Redeemer provide therapy to a Demon. Maybe let them use their Insight roll instead of a therapy roll? Or use it to give them some sort of bonus.<br /> <br /> Redeemers can also locate a &quot;source of hope&quot; for your Fallen. An item that you can draw faith from rather than your usual sources. I'd reward players who managed to sustain themselves without turning to what must surely feel like a parasitic relationship with humanity.<br /> <br /> Someone might say &quot;What about Martyr's Expiate?&quot; No. No way that it can work on a demon if it can't work on a changeling or wraith.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> the Shaman ability to summon the spirit of your targets mental sickness and do battle with it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know what some of this stuff is... but this? I would totally be okay with. If you can cast something upon a Demon to create an incarnate monster of the Torment and sins and horrible mistakes that torment you, and do battle with it? You could come to terms with your past actions. I'd allow it once per character, and let it remove one or two points of Permanent Torment depending on how challenging a fight it is. Of course.... the creature that manifests as a result of your Torment should be more horrible if your Torment is higher. I don't know how that mechanic works for shamans, but first I'd take whatever is in the rules already for that and then apply to that creature your fallen's high Torment Apocalyptic form atop it. Possibly more buffs as well...<br /> <br /> One more thing...<br /> <br /> P'o. P'o is some nasty stuff, and it's got a lot of similarities to Torment. If you find any powers or abilities that can reduce someone's permanent P'o rating, I'd suggest it could work to reduce Torment as well.<br /> <br /> However... once a character has hit Torment 10... they're really pretty much gone. The Earthbound are Torment 10, and NOTHING can change them. They are beyond help, in part because they are beyond this world and have lost all those things which they care about enough to come back for. If you and your players can make a compelling story about how they and their characters could make a heartfelt plea to their Torment 10 friend.... treat him as having 10 Temporary Torment. If you as a team can lower his Torment to 9 using the rules, then congrats. But I think this is effectively impossible. If the former character had any of the Best Friend or True Love merits, or things of that nature? Then I'd give bonuses for using them. Unfortunately.... 10 Torment is just... you're gone. That isn't your friend any more, they exist trapped in the mental reality of everything they've done wrong and everything they've lost. They are rage and murder and madness incarnate, and if your friend could see what he or she had become... well, your actions would be welcomed in stopping it for good.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6883-darkexcalibur42","name":"DarkExcalibur42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6883_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T22:54:53-07:00","id":590941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkExcalibur42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/576765-ways-other-splats-can-reduce-torment?p=590826#post590826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">P'o. P'o is some nasty stuff, and it's got a lot of similarities to Torment. If you find any powers or abilities that can reduce someone's permanent P'o rating, I'd suggest it could work to reduce Torment as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Demon Hunter X has a system for buying off points of it accumulated through Humanity loss and botched Conscience rolls, and it's possibly for Hungry Dead to raise their Hun and presumably shift a point from maximum paired Soul Virtues from P'o to Hun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T23:15:52-07:00","id":590957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/576765-ways-other-splats-can-reduce-torment?p=590941#post590941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Demon Hunter X has a system for buying off points of it accumulated through Humanity loss and botched Conscience rolls, and it's possibly for Hungry Dead to raise their Hun and presumably shift a point from maximum paired Soul Virtues from P'o to Hun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Demon Hunter X's system for buying it off is &quot;pay 10 XP, remove one point&quot;. So similarly costed to Torment. Unless there's another way that I forgot...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6883-darkexcalibur42","name":"DarkExcalibur42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6883_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}